# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20: the posse at the post office door. Doris holds a forged letter; they are charmed. Talk, run, give up or fight.

~ start
Narrator: Torches and heavy cudgels crowd the narrow lane, smelling of pitch and sour wool. Doris Squire stands in front, holding up a folded letter like a warrant.
doris_squire [angry]: This letter names you the postmaster's killers. Hands up, come along quiet, or we take you down by force.
-> menu

~ menu
* [Insight DC 18] Study Doris's eyes and the faces crowded behind her. -> charm | charm_missed
* [if flag.rk_charm_seen] [Persuasion DC 18] Tell Doris the letter is forged and her mind isn't her own. -> talk_down | talk_fail
* [if flag.rk_charm_seen] [Deception DC 18] Swear we found the body and blame Geneva instead. -> talk_down | talk_fail
* [Intimidation DC 20] Warn her what this mob will cost her if they step closer. -> talk_down | talk_fail
* [knows:dispel_magic] Cast Dispel Magic on Doris. -> spell
* [knows:remove_curse] Cast Remove Curse on Doris. -> spell
* Bolt down the east alley behind the post office. -> flee
* Put our hands up and go with them quietly. -> surrender
* Draw weapons and fight our way through. -> fight

~ charm
set rk_charm_seen
Narrator: A flat lilac glint sits in every single eye, steady and unblinking in the torchlight. This posse isn't angry, friends: it's being walked on a leash.
-> menu
~ charm_missed
Narrator: All you can make out in the smoky glare is a press of grim, tight-jawed faces that came straight from the supper table.
-> menu

~ talk_fail
doris_squire [angry]: No. Take them.
-> menu_after_fail

~ menu_after_fail
* [knows:dispel_magic] Cast Dispel Magic on Doris. -> spell
* [knows:remove_curse] Cast Remove Curse on Doris. -> spell
* Bolt down the east alley behind the post office. -> flee
* Put our hands up and go with them quietly. -> surrender
* Draw weapons and fight our way through. -> fight

~ talk_down
set posse_outcome = "talked"
set rk_posse_done
quest roving_rookery hysteria
doris_squire [weary]: Wait a minute, this hand isn't right. I've seen those grey birds watching the roofs too, so you get one hour, no more.
Narrator: The crowd shuffles slowly back toward the Round, their boots scraping the cobbles as they keep up a low chant. The fever hasn't broken, only paused.
-> END

~ spell
set posse_outcome = "talked"
set rk_posse_done
set doris_cleared
quest roving_rookery hysteria
Narrator: The spell runs over her like a bucket of well water, and the lilac shine drains right out of her eyes. For the next hour, Doris Squire is her own woman.
doris_squire [neutral]: Bah, this ink reeks of wet pigeon feathers. Get moving, quick now, before that purple fog creeps back into my head.
-> END

~ flee
set posse_outcome = "fled"
set rk_posse_done
quest roving_rookery hysteria
Narrator: You bolt down the dark alley, vault a splintered rail, and tear straight through somebody's winter cabbages. Their hoarse shouting chases your heels all the way to the estate road.
move wickermoor_village:from_estate

~ fight
set posse_outcome = "fought"
Narrator: Doris plants her heavy boots on the stones, and the deputies surge forward with their clubs raised.
combat rk_posse

~ surrender
set posse_outcome = "surrendered"
set rk_posse_done
set jail_began = now
quest roving_rookery jailed
doris_squire [neutral]: Gear on the stones, hands where I can see them. You get a cot and a bucket until the Witching Hour.
Narrator: The cell door is little more than an iron frame, though there's nowhere in Wickermoor left to run. Across the Round, you can already hear the mob chanting in the dark.
jail wickermoor_constable_station:cells until flag.jail_free

~ howie
howie_butterman [smile]: It'll go a whole lot easier on everyone if you just walk along quiet-like, friends. I can put a warm word in Doris's ear for a quick trial.
-> start

~ grunt
Narrator: A deputy in a linen armband stares straight through your shoulder, muttering your names under his breath in a slow, steady rhythm.
-> END
